The Old Working

Cave mouth

A low opening in the hillside, timbered on both sides. The timbers sag, and nobody has replaced them.
The air coming out is colder than the air going in.
You can see: brass lamp, short shovel.
Exits: in.
> take lamp
Taken.
> take shovel
Taken.
> light lamp
The wick catches. The light it gives is small, and it is enough.
> in
Debris room

Fallen roof, mostly, with the ends of props still sticking out of it. A passage leads down out of the far side, choked with rubble.
You can see: pile of rubble.
Exits: out, down.
> dig rubble
It comes away in handfuls, and then in a rush. The way down is open.
> down
Grotto

Water has been at this one a long while: the walls are grown over with something pale that throws the lamplight back.
Nothing has been dug here.
Exits: up.
> up
Debris room

Fallen roof, mostly, with the ends of props still sticking out of it. A passage leads down out of the far side, choked with rubble.
You can see: pile of rubble.
Exits: out, down.
> out
Cave mouth

A low opening in the hillside, timbered on both sides. The timbers sag, and nobody has replaced them.
The air coming out is colder than the air going in.
Exits: in.
> quit
Goodbye.
